ir crops. Their markets are disappearing because restaurants are closed. The Department of Agriculture didn't have logistics in place where it could redistribute the food to food banks where it was needed. Come on. I mean, you know, this is another thing we're finding. The government doesn't pay the attention of logistics. And there's a need to meet supply and demand. There's so many people out there who want to help, and yet the government doesn't seem to be able to, at every level, to be able to effectively utilize the resources that are already out there, let alone to take steps to create the resources that come from the natural inherent wealth of the American",
