  {
    "episode_id": 91237,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/1/91237.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 67,
    "turn_text": "When people say, well, if you go back too soon, you're going to hurt the economy. Well, our health is our wealth, each individual. But health is also, it's emotional health. It's physical, of course, it's spiritual. It's trying to stay aligned with moral and ethical principles that can guide us from one day to the next. The health and wealth are interchangeable. And we have a long way to go as a nation before we truly absorb that lesson. And so I'm concerned for our country, Rob. I'm concerned that We're looking at an America where the system set up to accelerate the wealth upwards, where the bailouts have increased the value of financialization, but not the value of real work, where we now realize those people we call essential prior to this COVID virus pandemic. People were looked out upon, but now we find out there are the very people who support our existence. they ought to be paid in recognition of that.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
