    "turn_idx": 78,
    "turn_text": "Well, it's always, and it's a core part of who we are, and that's what we learn. You know, it's interesting, our days under, in the non-pandemic period have been, you know, rounded by a ticking clock. And where we're at right now, and most of us who are working out of our homes, of course, we know there are people, police, fire, nurses, doctors, people working in supermarkets and other places who are in the job all the time. But those of us who are blessed with a little bit of time where we can work from the house, You know, we realize that time in some ways becomes elastic. And as our native friends know that time is essentially an illusion. And, you know, to be able to find that place where you can just become one with the sky and",
